-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/629108dc-bf09-5495-b6d6-f9f2338dcaec
-- title:
--   Test vectors with equal local integrals, one constant
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero prime $p$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, write $\mathbb{Q}_p =$ `p.adicCompletion ℚ` for the completion and $\psi =$ [`NumberField.StandardAddChar.psiLocal ℚ p`](def/LanglandsTunnell_StandardLocalConstantsAt.html#L65) for the local component at $p$ of the standard additive character; `LocalGL3 p` denotes $GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_p)$.
--
--   *Characters.* Four characters of $\mathbb{Q}_p^{\times}$ with values in $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ are given, each assumed unitary in the sense that all its values have absolute value $1$: a character $\omega_3$, a character $\chi$, a character $\xi$, and a character $\theta_0$. The hypothesis `hkp` asserts `HasConductorExponentAt ℚ p χ kp`, i.e. $\chi$ is trivial on the set of units $u$ with $v(u)=1$ and $v(u-1)\le q^{-k_p}$ (no second condition when $k_p=0$), while for every $m<k_p$ some unit in the corresponding set at level $m$ is not killed by $\chi$; likewise `hξB` asserts that $\xi$ has exact conductor exponent $B$ in this sense. For $\theta_0$ only triviality on the units $u$ with $v(u)=1$ and $v(u-1)\le q^{-b}$ is assumed (`hcθ`). A further natural number $f$ is given, carrying no condition of its own beyond the numerical and bump hypotheses below.
--
--   *The two $GL_3$ Whittaker vectors.* Functions $W_1, W_2 : GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_p)\to\mathbb{C}$ are given, each satisfying three conditions: the Whittaker transformation law `IsGL3PsiWhittakerFn` for $\psi^{-1}$, namely $W_i\!\left(\begin{pmatrix}1&x&z\\0&1&y\\0&0&1\end{pmatrix}g\right)=\psi(x+y)^{-1}W_i(g)$ for all $x,y,z\in\mathbb{Q}_p$ and all $g$; smoothness, in the form that some open subgroup of $GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ leaves $W_i$ invariant under right translation; and the central character law $W_i(t\cdot 1_3\, h)=\omega_3(t)W_i(h)$ for all $t\in\mathbb{Q}_p^{\times}$ and all $h$.
--
--   *Level hypotheses for the $\chi$-untwists.* Natural numbers $d_1,d_2$ are given together with `hlev1` and `hlev2`: for $i=1,2$ there exists a nonzero $W'$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace` $W_i$ — the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates $g\mapsto W_i(gh)$, $h\in GL_3(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ — such that for every $k$ in `localMaximalCompact3` (entries of $k$ and of $k^{-1}$ of valuation $\le 1$) all of whose entries satisfy $v(k_{ij}-\delta_{ij})\le q^{-d_i}$, the function $g\mapsto \chi(\det g)^{-1}W'(g)$ is invariant under right translation by $k$.
--
--   *The $GL_2$ partner.* An ideal $N\neq \bot$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ is given with $\mathfrak{p}^{b}\mid N$ and $\mathfrak{p}^{b+1}\nmid N$, and a function $w_{2,\mathrm{base}} : GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)\to\mathbb{C}$ subject to six hypotheses: the Whittaker law $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}\!\left(\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}g\right)=\psi(x)\,w_{2,\mathrm{base}}(g)$; right invariance under [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ p N`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178), the pullback under the local embedding $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)\to GL_2(\mathbb{A}^{\mathrm{fin}}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the adelic level-one subgroup of level $N$; non-vanishing $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}\neq 0$; an irreducibility clause, that every nonzero element $w$ of the span $V$ of the right translates of $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}$ has $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}$ in the span of the right translates of $w$; an admissibility clause, that for each open subgroup $U$ of $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ there is a finite set of functions whose span contains every right $U$-invariant element of $V$; and the central character law $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}(z\cdot 1_2\, g)=\theta_0(z)\,w_{2,\mathrm{base}}(g)$. An element $w_{0,p}\in GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ with underlying matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ is also given.
--
--   *Numerical thresholds.* The inequalities $2\max(d_1,d_2)+2\le B$, $B<k_p$, $f\le k_p$, $f+2\max(d_1,d_2)+3\le 2k_p$ and $2b+1\le k_p$ are assumed.
--
--   *Bump hypotheses.* For $i=1,2$, `hbump`$i$ asserts the existence of a $W_0$ in the cyclic subspace generated by the twisted function $g\mapsto \xi(\det g)\chi(\det g)^{-1}W_i(g)$ with four properties: $W_0$ is invariant under right translation by every element of the set `congruenceK1 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ p f`, consisting of those $k$ in `localMaximalCompact3` with $v(k_{20})$, $v(k_{21})$ and $v(k_{22}-1)$ all $\le q^{-f}$; the function $h\mapsto W_0(\iota(h))$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$, where $\iota =$ `iotaGL` is the embedding $h\mapsto \begin{pmatrix}h&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, is invariant under right translation by [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ p ⊤`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178); this function is supported in the set of products $\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}k$ with $x\in\mathbb{Q}_p$ and $k$ in that same subgroup; and $W_0(\iota(1))=1$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Equip $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra. Then there exist $w'$ in the span $V$ of the right translates of $w_{2,\mathrm{base}}$, $W_3$ in the cyclic subspace generated by $W_1$ and $W_3'$ in the cyclic subspace generated by $W_2$, such that for every Haar measure $\mu_2$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ and every Haar measure $\mu_{N_2}$ on the image of `unipotentGL2Hom`, i.e. on the upper unipotent subgroup $\{\begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}\}$, there is a real number $\sigma$ with the following three properties. Throughout, the Rankin–Selberg local integral is [`RSCarrier.rsLocalIntegral`](def/LanglandsTunnell_RSCarrier.html#L16) taken with respect to $\mu_2$, that unipotent subgroup and $\mu_{N_2}$, with modulus function $\delta(g)=|\det g|$ given by `modulus`, that is
--   $$\Psi(s;W,F)=\int (W(g)F(g))\,\delta(g)^{\,s-1/2}\,d\bigl(\mu_2.\mathrm{withDensity}\,(\mathrm{HaarQuotient.density})\bigr)(g).$$
--
--   First, for every $s$ with $\operatorname{Re} s>\sigma$,
--   $$\Psi\bigl(s;\,W_3\circ\iota,\,w'\bigr)=\Psi\bigl(s;\,W_3'\circ\iota,\,w'\bigr).$$
--
--   Secondly, for every $s$ with $\operatorname{Re} s>\sigma$ the same equality holds for the dual data,
--   $$\Psi\bigl(s;\,\widetilde{W_3}\circ\iota,\,\widetilde{w'}\bigr)=\Psi\bigl(s;\,\widetilde{W_3'}\circ\iota,\,\widetilde{w'}\bigr),$$
--   where $\widetilde{W}=$ `dualWhittakerFn3` $W$ is $g\mapsto W\bigl(w_3\cdot {}^{t}g^{-1}\bigr)$ with $w_3$ the antidiagonal permutation matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&0&1\\0&1&0\\1&0&0\end{pmatrix}$ in $GL_3$, and $\widetilde{w'}$ is the function $g\mapsto |\det g|\, w'\bigl(w_{0,p}\cdot {}^{t}g^{-1}\bigr)$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$.
--
--   Thirdly, there is a nonzero $\kappa\in\mathbb{C}$ such that at least one of the following holds: either $\Psi\bigl(s;\widetilde{W_3}\circ\iota,\widetilde{w'}\bigr)=\kappa$ for all $s$ with $\operatorname{Re} s>\sigma$, or $\Psi\bigl(s;W_3\circ\iota,w'\bigr)=\kappa$ for all such $s$. The assertion is thus that one of the two families of local integrals is constant on the half-plane, without specifying which.
--
--   This is the local stability statement in the $GL_3\times GL_2$ Rankin–Selberg theory used in the converse-theorem input to the Langlands–Tunnell theorem: after a sufficiently deeply ramified twist by $\chi$, two Whittaker vectors with the same central character admit common test vectors whose local integrals agree, and one of the two resulting integrals is a nonzero constant in $s$. It is cited by [`LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.exists_rsLocalIntegral_clearedFE_datum_of_centralChar_eq_of_deepTwist_pairStability32_of_bump`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.exists_rsLocalIntegral_clearedFE_datum_of_centralChar_eq_of_deepTwist_pairStability32_of_bump), where the constancy supplies the nonvanishing needed to clear the local functional equation.
